{"case_id":"T8009","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["missing format-specific corpus","missing direct API entry point","structured input-semantics gap"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["archive_read_support_format_rar","archive_read_format_rar_bid","archive_read_format_rar_read_header","read_header","read_exttime","read_symlink_stored","read_data_stored","archive_read_format_rar_read_data_skip"],"reason":"S1 adds an entire RAR reader and the public archive_read_support_format_rar API, but H0 has no RAR seed and never directly calls that API. Its sparse byte mutations of non-RAR archives are not a practical way to preserve the seven-byte RAR_SIGNATURE while generating the structured RAR headers, flags, sizes, filenames, timestamps, symlinks, and stored data needed to exercise the new parser deeply.","evidence":["H0's files[] contains ISO, CAB, LZH, tar, zip, ar, cpio, RPM, mtree, and compressed variants, but no .rar input.","H0 only calls archive_read_support_format_all; it contains no explicit call to the newly declared archive_read_support_format_rar.","archive_read_format_rar_bid requires memcmp(p, RAR_SIGNATURE, 7) == 0 before returning a positive bid.","H0 mutates fewer than approximately 1% of bytes in existing non-RAR seed files, so reaching RAR_SIGNATURE and coherent MAIN_HEAD, FILE_HEAD, NEWSUB_HEAD, and ENDARC_HEAD structures is implausible.","read_header parses attacker-controlled header_size, filename_size, FHD_LARGE, FHD_UNICODE, FHD_SALT, and FHD_EXTTIME fields, including malloc(filename_size) followed by filename[filename_size] = '\\0'.","read_symlink_stored uses attacker-controlled rar->packed_size in __archive_read_ahead and malloc, then writes filename[rar->packed_size] = '\\0'.","read_exttime advances p according to encoded flag nibbles, while read_data_stored and archive_read_format_rar_read_data_skip consume sizes derived from RAR headers."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated RAR harness or RAR corpus seeds that explicitly register archive_read_support_format_rar and exercise header iteration, data reads, and data skipping. Seed valid and truncated RARs covering MAIN_HEAD/FILE_HEAD/NEWSUB_HEAD, stored entries, large sizes, Unicode names, salts, extended times, symlinks, unsupported compression, encryption, and volume flags."}
